# Interview Prep Standards

Every `interview-prep.md` opens with this metadata header:

```markdown
**Company:** <Company>
**Role:** <Job Title>
**Phase:** <e.g. "1st Interview — HR/Recruiter Screen">
**Date:** <date/time with timezone>
**Type:** <Phone / Video / In-person> (<tool>)
**Attendee(s):** <Name — Title (email)>, one per line
```

Pull details from invite emails in `0 - Email/` when available; ask the user to fill gaps.

## Company Research (refresh each phase)

- Recent news and product announcements (last ~3–6 months)
- Financial health — earnings, funding, stock if public
- Sentiment — layoffs, leadership, breaches, awards (honest, both sides)
- 2–3 natural talking points

Do not reuse stale research from prior rounds.

## Equity

If equity/RSU language appears in posting or offer material, quote verbatim. Apply `.career-pipeline.yml` `compensation.equity_counts_toward_floor` and optional `compensation.notes` rather than inventing separate negotiation docs.

## 1st interview extras

Include salary benchmarking (sources noted, not presented as precise) and prepared strength/gap responses from the assessment under `1 - Application/` (basename from `naming.assessment`).
